# Protect the working launch

GTA V Enhanced Story Mode and LSPDFR now load. New features must not change that. After any change to launch, install, file mapping, BattlEye, permissions, or the duty folder layout, run `npm run verify` and fix failures before adding more work.

## Folders

- **Online / official Steam only:** never install mods, RPH, ASI, or LSPDFR here.
- **Duty sandbox:** `Grand Theft Auto V Enhanced - LSPDFR` is the only place mods and RPH live.
- Do not merge, swap, or write across these folders.

## Leave these flows alone unless a new log proves they are broken

- `src/services/launcher.js` `launchLspdfr` (repair layout, BattlEye off, RPH ini, materialize exes, elevate RPH)
- `src/services/installer.js` `repairLspdfrLayout`
- `src/services/modtypes.js` `RPH_ROOT_DLLS` and DLL remap rules
- `src/services/battleye.js` and `src/services/permissions.js`

Add new features in new files or UI when possible. Do not rewrite a working launch/install path to “clean it up.”

## Known-good duty layout

- `Plugins\` root may contain only `LSPD First Response.dll`, its `.config`, its `.pdb`, and the `Plugins\LSPDFR\` folder.
- Support DLLs (`LMS.Common`, `DiscordRpcNet`, `DdsConvert`, `SlimDX`, `EasyHook`, Gwen, Mono.Cecil, …) stay **next to the game exe**, not in `Plugins\`.
- Never put `LSPD First Response.dll` or `Newtonsoft.Json.dll` in the game root.
- Never overwrite `XInput1_4.dll` (ASI loader) with the small RPH hook copy.
- `startup.rphs` must stay `LoadPlugin "LSPD First Response.dll"` — never `ReloadAllPlugins`.
- `PluginTimeoutThreshold` must stay `60000`. RPH rejects `180000`.
- F4 is the RPH console (often invisible on Enhanced). Do not “fix” missing LSPDFR by changing F4.

## Do not do

- Drop extra DLLs into `Plugins\` (ReloadAllPlugins will treat them as plugins).
- Hand-edit Steam launch options (`-skipPatchChecker`, `-launchTitleInFolder`).
- Kill `RAGEPluginHook` / `GTA5_Enhanced` when restarting Electron if the user is in-game.
- Put mods in the official Steam folder.
- Re-add `Newtonsoft.Json.dll` to “help” LSPDFR (it is IL-merged and breaks load).
